<!--
  Monochrome (themed-icon) layer for the launcher icon, API 33+.

  This is the Knit mark as a POSITIVE silhouette: the "K" strokes fill, with the diamond node's
  inner cutout as a hole (single path, nonZero fill — the overlapping strokes must union, so
  evenOdd would punch holes at every crossing). Do not point the monochrome layer at
  drawable/ic_stat_mesh: that vector is the INVERSE mark (a filled rounded square with the K
  knocked out), correct for a notification status icon and a solid tinted blob here.

  The group transform places the glyph at exactly the position and scale of the raster
  mipmap/ic_launcher_foreground within the 108dp canvas, so the themed icon registers with the
  normal icon instead of drifting. Geometry stays inside the 72dp safe zone.

  No android:tint — the launcher supplies the tint for monochrome layers.
-->
